00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.980
This body language,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.480
these gestures...

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.010
"I'm currently looking for something,

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.670
so if you have some time,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.550
can you help me look, Oni-chan?"

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.800
That's what it means.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.300
Like I'd know!

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.640
So, how about it?

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.470
Are you going to help, or are you not going to help?

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.540
Be clear.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.040
I'd like to help,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.170
but to be blunt, the results of the multiple-choice test weren't too great.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.550
It seems that I have to boost it quite a bit from here on.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:06.240
Oni-chan, what were you doing for the past year?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.500
Why don't you just die?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.540
I'm not telling you to go study.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.270
You should just die.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.520
In any case, don't try to kill me.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:20.210
Until you help me with my search, I'll keep insulting you.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.670
I'll keep telling you to die.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:23.890
I give up.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.050
I'll help you.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.820
So, is what you're looking for around here somewhere?

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.660
Who knows?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.520
It's not necessarily in this area.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:37.480
Well, if you're saying it's not necessarily
in this area, let's look with that in mind.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.180
So, Ononoki-chan,

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.880
what is it I'm supposed to be looking for?

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.780
Who knows?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.010
I wonder what it is.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.530
Yay!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.780
Yay...

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.640
I was told I would know what I'm looking for when I saw it.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:56.400
While I'm searching for something I want your help

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.900
to spread my field of vision

00:03:59.170 --> 00:03:59.900
Field of vision?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.670
FIELD
OF
VISION

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.670
SPREAD

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.650
Well, I don't seem to be getting anywhere,

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.310
so I thought that I needed a change in point of view.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.930
As you can see, I'm a treasured doll after all.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.680
So I'm a bit short.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.050
In other words, I lack the vertical altitude to search for something.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.650
It's true that my point of view is slightly higher than yours,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.320
but that's only relatively speaking.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.070
If you're speaking in absolutes,
I'm not that tall either, you know?

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.500
I can see that.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.790
I can see that, even from a lower point of view,

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:36.080
you're definitely not one of the taller people.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.560
I meant in absolutes, not definites.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.380
But if you add Oni-chan's pretty short height to my really short height,

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.590
what a surprise, we end up with a height that's rather tall.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.570
To be specific, close to three meters.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:49.830
<i>I see.</i>

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.570
<i>It's an event to carry a girl on my shoulders.</i>

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.830
Ononoki-chan, let me confirm something.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.690
That means you want me to carry you on my shoulders, right?

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.410
That's not it, Oni-chan.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.840
I won't carry you on my shoulders,
and I won't let you carry me.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.030
Just think about it.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.970
There's too much of a loss if I sit on your shoulders, isn't there?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:07.970
A loss?

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.720
Oh, it's simple, Oni-chan.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.450
We just have to do what I always do.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.240
Hey, Ononoki-chan.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.320
For now, we can continue to search for whatever it is like this.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.200
You'll know what you're looking for when you see it,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.080
does that mean I'd know what it is when I see it, too?

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.570
I've been pushing my limits as a vampire lately,

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:42.610
so if you're expecting me to have an apparition's eyesight, I can't meet that.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.660
It's fine.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.480
I'm not expecting anything from you.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.060
In any case, even if it's not suspicious,

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.260
if there's anything that bothers you, or you feel is strange,

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:56.850
just report every occurrence to me and we're good.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:58.480
Good?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.760
It's not like I have a lot of free time, you know?

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.820
You mean how you only have six months left to live?

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.460
How much longer do you have?

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.890
Which happens first, your remaining days run out,
or your college entrance exams end?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.730
It's a close call.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.610
The college entrance exams will end first.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.920
And then the graduation ceremony is in the middle,

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.250
and I find out the results after that.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:29.130
When you say you've been pushing your limits
as a vampire, that's what it entails, right?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.040
You're still not only making useless efforts,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.980
but suffering useless defeats as well, right, Oni-chan?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.910
It's not necessarily useless.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.300
Hey, Oni-chan.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.520
What are you going to do from now on?

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:46.780
If you want, I don't mind contacting Gaen-san, you know?

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.820
But I went against her will, and didn't use that talisman.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.800
Considering that, I can't ask for her help now.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.570
Well, these are seeds I've sown.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.040
I'll do something about it.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:04.040
If they really are seeds you've sown,
you should indeed do something.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.710
But don't you think it's a bit strange?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.380
That recently, only things around you are falling into disarray,

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:12.050
as if something is keeping balance.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.810
Though meeting an apparition
makes you drawn to apparitions.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.430
It seems like even that balance is being taken from you.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:23.190
I don't think you're so dense that you wouldn't feel how unnatural it is.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.020
I'm dense.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:28.710
I'm always doing everything I can to patch up the current situation.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.710
Something you'd know is what you're looking for when you see it.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.200
I wonder what that is?

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.350
Who knows?

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.450
TN: "The Spinning Dancer" by Nobuyuki Kayahara

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.720
Even if you ask me that, I have no idea.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:49.310
But Oni-chan, I sometimes think of what it might be.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.860
Oh. What is it?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:54.360
Something that anyone would know
what it is when they see it,

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.350
but something you lose sight of when you look for it.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:58.910
That's...

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:06.860
a smile.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.530
<i>What you'd call an epilogue, or the punch line for this episode.</i>

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:16.530
<i>In the end, we wandered all over town until sunset,</i>

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.040
<i>but we couldn't find anything, and nothing was achieved.</i>

