HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:27.290
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:27.290
<i>What do you think is the hardest thing to look for?</i>

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:29.300
What are you talking about?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.060
I'm talking about Ononoki-chan's story.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:35.550
Araragi-kun, you're going to live together with Ononoki-chan, right?

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:39.050
If so, I thought I should tell you about that.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.810
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.810
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.810
<i>What do you think is the hardest thing to look for?</i>

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.030
Let's see...

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.810
The hardest thing to find that I can think of...

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.470
No, this question is just a preface,

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.690
so how you think and what you answer really don't matter.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:58.200
Then, what question are you going to ask after this preface?

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.200
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.200
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.200
<i>That would be, "What do you think is the easiest thing to find?"</i>

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:07.580
Of course, I think that would be something "you'd know when you see it."

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.410
No, Araragi-kun.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.340
Don't be so bound to those words.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.340
Because that's a lie.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.840
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.840
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.840
<i>A lie?</i>

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.940
Calling it a lie may be too much,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:20.870
but Ononoki-chan wasn't looking for anything.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:25.870
The hardest thing to look for is,
well, something of that sort.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.100
You can't find something that doesn't exist.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:34.030
Can it be that Ononoki-chan told such an innocent lie
because she wanted to play with me?

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.280
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.280
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.280
<i>That's not it.</i>

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:35.900
<b>SIMPLY</b>

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:35.950
<b>SIMPLY</b>

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:36.070
<b>DENIED</b>

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:36.110
<b>DENIED</b>

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:36.150
<b>DENIED</b>

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:36.780
<b>DENIED</b>

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.410
That answer is the "easiest thing to find."

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.420
Of course, something easy to find
is something that stands out.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.080
So what stands out?

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.380
Nothing stands out more than someone looking for something.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:55.130
Stopping in your tracks, looking around,
bending down, standing on your tiptoes.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.760
No matter what you do, you end up acting suspiciously.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:03.620
Standing on the finger of a girl who looks like a doll
and looking for something from so high up.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.770
That alone is a rather noticeable act, right?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.520
<b>CONSPICUOUS</b>

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:06.580
<b>CONSPICUOUS</b>

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:06.680
<b>STANDS OUT</b>

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:06.730
<b>STANDS OUT</b>

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:06.770
<b>STANDS OUT</b>

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:07.520
<b>STANDS OUT</b>

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:13.290
So Ononoki-chan's plan was to make you stand out.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:17.280
And so, she hoisted you up like a flag.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.530
But why did Ononoki-chan want me to stand out?

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:27.160
In January, there was someone in that town
you weren't supposed to meet, right?

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:33.750
<i>Someone you weren't supposed to meet,
and who didn't want to see you, either.</i>

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.130
<b>THOUGH, IN THE END, I DID BUMP INTO HIM.</b>

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:38.880
That someone was visiting the town virtually every day,

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.510
so I don't think it would've been strange
to pass by him at some point.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:46.890
But Ononoki-chan probably prevented it from happening.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:51.650
By making you stand out, Araragi-kun,
it made it easier for him to avoid you.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:55.170
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:55.170
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.150
<i>By making me search for something I couldn't find,</i>

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.620
she made it easy to find me.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.400
<i>So that the con artist and I</i>

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.700
<i>wouldn't have a close encounter.</i>

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.610
In Ononoki-chan's mind, she didn't want you to feel

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:10.160
any more anxious than you already did back then.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.120
I'm sure.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:16.920
Nothing happening, no incidents,
a situation with no story to tell is,

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:21.430
surprisingly enough, supported by things
like someone's thoughtfulness.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:28.450
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:28.450
ARARAGI KOYOMI

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:26.320
<i>Not realizing that my peaceful life was supported by something,</i>

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.450
<i>I tried to do something on my own.</i>

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.360
That is indeed a bit humorous.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.980
No wonder she ridiculed me.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.620
Perhaps.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:38.940
"People just help themselves out on their own" is a great phrase,

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:44.220
but in reality, it's impossible to live all on your own.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.260
Well, yeah.

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:50.700
Normally, you don't think about stuff like that
at all while living your everyday life.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.620
Right.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:56.950
Perhaps such nonchalant acts of thoughtfulness

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:00.070
are the hardest things to find.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:27.950
<b>Nayami ketobashite ishi ga korogatte ku</b>

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:27.950
<b>Kicking a stone as if I was kicking my troubles</b>

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:33.710
<b>Sukoshi gomakashita are wa shigatsu no koto</b>

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:33.710
<b>It was April when I played my trick</b>

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:39.170
<b>Koukishin ousei de akarui kodomo deshita</b>

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:39.170
<b>I was a curious and cheerful child</b>

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:44.930
<b>Senaka oshita no wa ano hi kara no boku de</b>

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:44.930
<b>The me from the past gave me a push</b>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:50.810
<b>Hamidasenai retsu wo oinuite</b>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:50.810
<b>Let's loiter on the way</b>

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:56.400
<b>Michikusa wo shiyou</b>

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:56.400
<b>Passing a line you can't even lean out from</b>

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:04.070
<b>Kago ni nose taisetsu na yume</b>

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:04.070
<b>I'll put my precious dreams in the basket</b>

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:09.450
<b>pedaru mawashi tooku made saa mochi dasou</b>

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:09.450
<b>and spin the pedals, carrying them far away!</b>

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:14.830
<b>Uwasa shita boku no mirai wa</b>

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:14.830
<b>My rumored future...</b>

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.620
<b>Kokochi iino?</b>

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.620
<b>Am I comfortable with it?</b>

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.920
<b>Nobiru kage ni kiitemo</b>

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.920
<b>I even asked my long shadow;</b>

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:28.760
<b>Wakaranai wakaranai wakaranai</b>

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.960
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.720
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.760
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>
